{
  "id": "1395",
  "slug": "count-number-of-teams",
  "title": "Count Number of Teams",
  "category": "dsa",
  "subcategory": "dynamic-programming",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "Dynamic Programming",
    "Binary Indexed Tree",
    "Segment Tree"
  ],
  "statement": "There are `n` soldiers standing in a line. Each soldier is assigned a **unique** `rating` value.\n\nYou have to form a team of 3 soldiers amongst them under the following rules:\n\n*   Choose 3 soldiers with index (`i`, `j`, `k`) with rating (`rating[i]`, `rating[j]`, `rating[k]`).\n*   A team is valid if: (`rating[i] < rating[j] < rating[k]`) or (`rating[i] > rating[j] > rating[k]`) where (`0 <= i < j < k < n`).\n\nReturn the number of teams you can form given the conditions. (soldiers can be part of multiple teams).\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: rating = [2,5,3,4,1]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: We can form three teams given the conditions. (2,3,4), (5,4,1), (5,3,1).\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: rating = [2,1,3]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: We can't form any team given the conditions.\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: rating = [1,2,3,4]\nOutput: 4\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `n == rating.length`\n*   `3 <= n <= 1000`\n*   `1 <= rating[i] <= 10^(5)`\n*   All the integers in `rating` are **unique**.",
  "constraints": [
    "n == rating.length",
    "3 <= n <= 1000",
    "1 <= rating[i] <= 105",
    "All the integers in rating are unique."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "rating = [2,5,3,4,1]",
      "output": "3",
      "explanation": "We can form three teams given the conditions. (2,3,4), (5,4,1), (5,3,1)."
    },
    {
      "input": "rating = [2,1,3]",
      "output": "0",
      "explanation": "We can't form any team given the conditions."
    },
    {
      "input": "rating = [1,2,3,4]",
      "output": "4",
      "explanation": null
    }
  ],
